6️⃣ DHCP

DHCP = Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol

It automatically provides network configuration to a host.

It can provide:

IP address

Subnet mask

Default gateway

DNS server information

Lease information



---

7️⃣ Why DHCP?

Without DHCP, you could manually configure:

IP
Subnet Mask
Gateway
DNS

DHCP automates this.


---

8️⃣ DHCP Process — DORA ⭐

Memorize:

DORA

D → Discover
O → Offer
R → Request
A → Acknowledge


---

Step 1 — DHCP Discover

Client broadcasts:

> "Is there a DHCP server?"



Client
  ↓
DHCP Discover
  ↓
Broadcast


---

Step 2 — DHCP Offer

DHCP server offers an IP configuration.

Server
  ↓
DHCP Offer
  ↓
Client


---

Step 3 — DHCP Request

Client requests the offered configuration.

Client
  ↓
DHCP Request
  ↓
Server


---

Step 4 — DHCP ACK

Server confirms the allocation.

Server
  ↓
DHCP ACK
  ↓
Client


---

🔥 9️⃣ DORA Diagram

Client                         DHCP Server

   DHCP DISCOVER
   ─────────────────────────→

                  DHCP OFFER
   ←─────────────────────────

   DHCP REQUEST
   ─────────────────────────→

                  DHCP ACK
   ←─────────────────────────

Remember:

> Discover → Offer → Request → Acknowledge




