2️⃣6️⃣ Network Addressing Journey

Suppose you enter:

www.example.com

What happens?

Step 1

DNS resolves:

Domain → IP

Step 2

Your computer determines whether destination is local or remote.

Step 3

If remote, it sends the frame toward the default gateway.

Step 4

ARP may resolve:

Gateway IP → Gateway MAC

Step 5

Ethernet frame carries the IP packet to the router.

Step 6

Routers forward the packet toward the destination.


